{# The area's tab strip — drawn by the shell, from the one source that decides it.

   This file is a forwarding address and nothing else. The strip's markup and its
   rules (underlined siblings, exactly one lit, a withheld screen absent rather
   than greyed) belong to uhifadhi/shell-module; which screens this area has and
   which of them the viewer may reach belongs to Uhifadhi\Navigation\AreaShellSource,
   which the sidebar's location tree reads too. Neither is decided here, and the
   `active` parameter every caller used to pass is gone: the source resolves the
   current request itself, so a page can no longer name the wrong tab.

   It survives at all because a dozen pages include it by hand. A page that
   extends '@UhifadhiShell/page.html.twig' does not need it — the frame renders
   the strip by default, which is why a module's page keeps the area's tabs
   instead of losing them. #}
{{ include('@UhifadhiShell/_area_tabs.html.twig', {tabs: shell_tabs()}, with_context: false) }}
